OUTPUTS: every place it sends bitcoin.
CHANGE: the part returned to your own verified address.
TXID: the tracking ID used after broadcast.
FEE RATE: fee paid per unit of transaction size.
LOCKTIME: the earliest block it may confirm in.
DERIVATION PATH: the standard branch used to find a key.
DESCRIPTOR: a read only address map. it cannot spend.␀␀␀NOT FOUND IN FIRST %u ADDRESSES␀valid for this network, but outside the first 100 receiving/change addresses searched. this is not definitive.␀␀WRONG NETWORK␀␀␀this address is valid, but for the other Bitcoin network. switch networks or scan again.␀␀␀␀INVALID ADDRESS␀the address format or checksum is invalid. do not use it.␀␀␀Looking for the QR code␀point the camera at the screen showing it␀␀␀Found it: hold steady␀␀␀Too much packed into this QR␀␀␀␀ask your coordinator for an animated QR␀Move back a little␀␀part of the code is out of view␀Reading␀Point at something with detail␀␀books, a plant, your desk: not a blank wall␀Looking good: tap to capture␀␀␀␀the photo mixes with chip randomness to make your words␀x close␀of␀␀STORAGE␀COORDINATOR WATCHES + CREATES THE PSBT␀␀KISS CHECKS + SIGNS THE PSBT␀␀␀␀COORDINATOR BROADCASTS THE TRANSACTION␀␀WHAT IS A SEED?␀YOUR SEED PHRASE␀␀␀␀12 or 24 ordered words, called a BIP39 mnemonic␀those words plus your passphrase are what make your wallet. not this device.

write both down and any compatible BIP39 signer or wallet app can rebuild it, even if this device is lost.

the words alone rebuild a different wallet: the one with no passphrase.␀␀␀UNDERLINE␀␀␀LINE ABOVE␀␀LINE THROUGH␀␀␀␀CIRCLE IT␀␀␀TICK␀␀␀␀TWO WAYS IN␀one opens your wallet. one opens a wallet you can afford to show.␀␀␀drawing KISS opens a spare wallet with no passphrase asked for.

add one more stroke after the word and it asks for your passphrase and opens your real wallet instead.

nobody watching can tell the spare from the only one.␀␀PUT A LITTLE IN THE SPARE␀␀␀the spare wallet has its own fingerprint and really works.

send a small amount to it. an empty wallet on a signer looks like a wallet somebody is hiding something behind.␀YOUR STROKE␀draw KISS, then this, to reach your real wallet␀DRAW IT␀draw your stroke on the word below␀␀ONCE MORE␀␀␀the same stroke again, so a slip now does not lock you out later␀␀␀␀THAT WAS NOT IT␀nothing was saved.

try the stroke again, or go back
and pick a different one.␀␀NOT NOW␀BOTH WAYS IN ARE SET␀␀␀␀KISS on its own opens the spare wallet.

KISS with your stroke asks for your passphrase and opens your real one.

